<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs bar Telecom rise as Dow rises 12.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs bar Telecom rise as Dow rises 12.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apart from Telecom, New Zealand ADRs were firmer as the Dow gained 12.7 to 6286.9 by 7.45 a.m. NZT.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$27 3/8	 +0 3/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$29 1/4	 +0 5/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	 N.Y.    US$18 1/2	 +0 1/8  *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16 1/8	 -0 1/8  *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$85 5/8	 -2	*</p>
<p>Tranz Rail   N.Y.    US$17 1/2	 nil     *</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  167		 +2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  34		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  28		  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  242		 untraded</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  152 1/4	   -0 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  129 1/2	   -1 3/4</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.33	    nil</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.48	    -1</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$3.20	    +5</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
